            <lido:descriptiveNoteValue xml:lang="en">
              This painting captures the Rhône River at night, under a swirling sky filled with stars. 
              Van Gogh was particularly fascinated by night scenes and the challenge of painting in the dark.
              The work shows the artist's distinctive style with bold colors and dynamic brushstrokes.
            </lido:descriptiveNoteValue>
          </lido:objectDescriptionSet>
          <lido:objectDescriptionSet lido:type="provenance">
            <lido:descriptiveNoteValue>
              1889: Theo van Gogh, Paris; 
              1891: Johanna van Gogh-Bonger, Bussum; 
              1925: V.W. van Gogh, Laren; 
              1962: Vincent van Gogh Foundation; 
              1973: on permanent loan to Van Gogh Museum
            </lido:descriptiveNoteValue>
          </lido:objectDescriptionSet>
        </lido:objectDescriptionWrap>
        
